WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.338
Apophis passes the Earth.

00:03.038 --> 00:05.748
One pass is already in the calendar.

00:06.198 --> 00:21.293
This rock, Apophis, is about three hundred and forty metres across, and this is the evening it comes closest: about thirty-two thousand kilometres above the ground, inside the ring of satellites that carry television.

00:21.743 --> 00:23.007
It will miss.

00:23.457 --> 00:29.166
The path drawn here is the one predicted at NASA's Jet Propulsion Laboratory.
